            <ArticleTitle>Nonopioid analgesics.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>97-111</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>NSAIDs are useful analgesics for many pain states, especially those involving inflammation. Their use is frequently overlooked in patients with postoperative and chronic pain. Unless there is a contraindication, the use of an NSAID should be routinely considered to manage acute pain, chronic cancer, and noncancer pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
